course: dictionary
lesson: 2426
title: Context clues in science words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some science words are hard because you rarely hear them at home. Context helps you work out the meaning. «When fighting an infection the immune system releases chemical messengers, called cytokines, that make you sleepy so the body can save energy.» The words «called» and «messengers» are your clues: a cytokine is a kind of message.
explain: Check your guess by swapping in your meaning. "The immune system releases chemical messengers, called tiny messages, that make you sleepy" still makes sense, so your guess is close. The dictionary adds the exact science: a cytokine is a tiny protein that cells send out as a message.
explain: The sentence also tells you what cytokines do: they make you sleepy so the body can save energy. You do not need every science detail to understand how the body fights back.
fact: A cytokine is a tiny protein.
fact: Cells send cytokines out as a message.
fact: Cytokines help control the immune system when the body fights germs.
fact: «Cytokines» can make you feel tired or sleepy, which helps the body save energy.
fact: You may hear the word cytokine in news about illnesses and vaccines.
exercise: What is a cytokine? | A medicine you swallow with water | A bone that holds up the arm | A type of germ that makes you ill | *A tiny protein that cells send out as a message
exercise: «...that make you sleepy so the body can save energy.» What do cytokines do here? | They stop all messages in the body | *They can make you feel sleepy | They make you grow taller overnight | They make you run much faster
exercise: Which word in «chemical messengers, called cytokines» is the best clue that a cytokine is a kind of message? | infection | *messengers | energy | sleepy
test: «When you have a cold, cells release cytokines to call immune cells to fight the infection.» In this sentence, what are cytokines doing? | Fighting with the cold | *Sending a message to call immune cells | Making cold air | Breaking the skin
test: Which meaning fits best? A cytokine is a ___ that cells send out. | a germ | a bone | *a message | a colour
exam: Mia reads a science text and meets cytokine. What should she do first? | Give up and never read science again | Guess it is a kind of bird and move on | Skip the whole text without reading any more | *Read the words around it for clues, then check a dictionary if still unsure
